notes.content:
Hello again! I apologize for the long delay between updates.

Week 2 focuses on completing Work Orders. They are where you build signs to required specifications to earn experience points for leveling up. The leveling system is barebones as of this update, but there are at least some achievements tied to leveling up.

Update version 1.2.0 notes:
[list]
[*]Week 2 gameplay;

[*]10 new achievements;

[*]Added new Job type: Work Orders! Use the Work Order folder to complete Work Orders. These orders are specifications for creating signs, such as sign faces and vinyl types, quantity, measurements, etc. You can view the sign blueprint for help with building the sign;

[*]More sound effects for actions/menus;

[*]Level Up/Exp gained widgets;

[*]Saw cut size menu. If you use the primary action key on the base of either the wall saw or drop saw, a menu will open. This menu allows you to set what measurement you want the cut to be at. This makes it much easier to cut materials.

[*]New Material: White Aluminum Sheet Metal. These can be used as sign faces. They are the ones that have a pink plastic backing;

[*]Added level blockers to prevent objects from escaping the bounds of the fence;

[*]New Equipment: Phone. When a work order is selected, use the phone to order vinyl for the job. Located on the desk that has the Basic Task and Work Order folders;

[*]New Equipment: Time Clock. Use this to clock out and progress to the next work day/week. Located by the desk that has the Basic Task and Work Order folders;

[*]New Equipment: Sign Zone. This is in the shop's middle room. Use this area to complete Work Orders. Place a sign that has passed evaluation in the zone. Interact with the zone. If the sign disappears, it was successfully completed;

[*]New Equipment: Frame Zone. This is also in the shop's middle room. When a frame is welded, place the frame in the zone and interact with the zone. If a Work Order is selected, and the frame is the right size, it will align the frame to the proper set up;

[*]Made vinyl application easier. Now the sprays don't dissipate as fast;

[*]Clipboard tool new ability: Sign Frame Aligning! 

First you need a Work Order in progress that requires a sign frame. With the clipboard tool held, switch to the sign blueprint by using the tool mode change button.  Defaults are "[" and "]" keys. With a metal frame constructed, right click the sign. This aligns the frame properly and will allow the Work Order to be completed correctly.

[*]Clipboard tool new ability: Sign Evaluation!

With a Work Order in progress, and the clipboard tool held, right click the sign to see if it passes or fails the Work Order specifications. Make sure the Work Order is displayed on the clipboard. Press the tool mode change button if necessary. Defaults are "[" and "]" keys;

[*]Fixed sign frame wonkiness. Now it is easier and smoother to pick up, manipulate and move frames;

[*]Updated some tutorials. Added two new tutorials for Sign Fabrication and Work Orders;

[*]Added a white border to the screw mouse cursor, for better visibility;

[*]Adjusted shop layout: Drill and screws now on table with welding tool. Made Vinyl table a little bigger;

[*]Fixed glitch where removing objects from a rack or saw would mess with proper functioning of the object's physics;

[*]Fixed Clipboard glitch where Basic Task screen would get scrunched up;

[*]Object description widget now shows metal bar size converted to units used, such as inches or centimeters. It also now shows the type of vinyl a vinyl print is. Example: "Vinyl Print - Main Logo";

[*]Welder tool uses spool wire at a slower rate, deducts every 2 seconds instead of every 1;

[*]Adjusted drop saw model blade to be oriented how it would be in real life [lol]. Other improvements to wall saw and drop saw to make them work smoother;

[*]Various other glitch fixes and improvements;

[/list]

Thanks for checking out these notes. And thanks for your support!

This update adds week 1 gameplay to Job Mode! You essentially go from Monday to Friday, completing Basic Tasks. When you have completed the amount of tasks that you want, you can "clock out" and progress to the next day. You earn experience from completing the tasks. Currently just week 1 gameplay is available, with Friday being the last day. The current idea for Job Mode is to start off completing Basic Tasks, leveling up your character and then later completing more complex tasks and Work Orders (building signs to specifications).

[list]
[*]Added Week 1 gameplay to Job Mode;

[*]7 new achievements;

[*]Drop saw and wall saw fixes;

[*]Job stats tracking, sweeping, tasks, etc;

[*]New Player Menu, includes Player Stats and Job stats;

[*]Additional Basic Tasks programming;

[*]Evaluation Pallet equipment, this is for placing cut materials on to evaluate if their size is correct;

[*]Improved Dialogue System and more dialogue for Shop Cat;

[*]Weed cutter tool for Grass Cutting Task;

[*]Grass object for Grass Cutting Task;

[*]New controls menu buttons, hotkeys (will implement their use later);

[*]Metal frame now has object description and better highlighting;

[*]Cancel task widget to avoid accidentally cancelling a task in progress;

[*]Time clock (for seeing current day/week and total weekly tasks) and Progress widget (for progressing to next day);

[*]Improvements to widgets;

[*]Tolerance on cut sizes for cutting tasks, for 0 difficulty tasks, you can be off by 0.25" or 0.635cm of required measurement. Example: Need 96", but
material is 95.75" (within tolerance so it will pass evaluation) 

[*]Fixed wall saw rack glitch with not being able to remove a sign face when interacting with the saw's base;

[*]Material evaluation green/red pulse to signal material pass/fail task evaluation;

[*]Task object green pulse to signify which objects are related to current task;

[*]Leveling and experience system (you can earn experience from tasks to gain levels, system not fully implemented yet);

[*]Reorganized the shop a bit;

[*]Added to job system Basic Tasks tutorial;

[*]Hill's propane vinyl texture upgrade;

[*]Bonus text on task object completion widget, e.g. when you throw away trash for a task it appears as a +1 (can be turned off);

[*]Many new template widgets, borders, buttons, boxes, etc;

[*]Task menu got an upgrade;

[*]Various other fixes;
[/list]
Thanks for your interest and support!

Sorry for the delay between updates. This one includes just a few things added to the environment, the early state of a new mode, a shop cat to introduce the mode, updated menu visuals, updated font, some other widget changes and bug fixing. I've been working on some behind the scenes stuff for the new mode that isn't quite ready yet.

[list]

[*]Job Mode! This is quite barebones right now, but I will try to get another update out for it soon. Currently there is just a little introduction and you can view the design of the basic tasks menu.

The plan for this mode is to start with completing basic tasks (sweeping, trash collecting, material preparation, etc.) at first. Work orders (specifications for signs to build) will be included later on;

[*]A shop cat has been included! She will introduce the new mode. I added one achievement for it;

[*]Added a Job Mode menu where you can start, load and delete save files;

[*]New environment equipment: Ice Maker, Fridge, Adjustable (and spinnable) Office Chair and a Utility Sink;

[*]You can now see the name of pickup objects when you mouse over them. This can be turned off by setting "Object Description" to false in the options menu;

[*]New look for dialogue menus;

[*]Menu design updates and font updated (includes lower case now);

[*]A few other improvements, such as now the broom tool can change modes with the right click. For maximum sweeping efficiency;

[*]Various glitch fixes;
[/list]
Thanks for checking the game out and your support!

Hey there! Next update I plan on trying to add more to the shop's environment and the sign building system.
[list]

[*]In the shop there is now an arcade cabinet, where you can play a silly sandwich making mini-game;

[*]A microwave has been also added to the shop to for added realism;

[*]7 new achievements relating to the microwave and arcade cabinet;
 
[*]Fixed problems with tool progress bar when sweeping dust;

[*]Fixed glitch where sign face wasn't going transparent when highlighted while placed on frame (for easier drilling of screws into both face and frame);

[*]Fixed glitches with custom key binding where sometimes keys weren't getting properly swapped/removed;

[*]Fixed glitches with how sign face with vinyl is screwed onto sign frame;

[*]Now object actions widget correctly shows custom keys set for primary, secondary and scroll and override key;

[*]Various other fixes/improvements;
[/list]

Thanks for checking it out!

Hello again! Added one new achievement, with plans to add more!

[list]
[*]New Tool: Angle Grinder (Allows you to shave miniscule lengths off of a metal tube. Intended to be easier than using the saw for small cuts);

[*]New Tool Item: Metal Blending Wheel (for use with Angle Grinder);

[*]New Tool: Broom! 

There are two tool modes (use the '[' and ']' keys to switch modes) for this tool!

  >Sweep Forward: when using this mode, the broom points forward and when you use it, it will send trashballs/dust piles flying! Single click action.

  >Sweep Downward: this mode allows you to 'clean up' dust piles until they are gone! Click and hold to sweep continuously!

[*]New Object: Dust piles! These can be swept up for immense satisfaction (as well as a cool achievement). These metal shavings spawn when you cut metal on the saw or use the angle grinder on an aluminum tube.

[*]Improved physics for pickup objects. For example, sometimes objects would get a weird rotation on racking. Metal tube physics on the Y axis are now working right;

[*]New textures for: Wall Saw, Drop Saw, Impact Drill and Spoolgun Welder;

[*]Fixed a glitch that caused "Tool Mode Previous" key from being unable to be set;

[*]And some various random glitch fixing and improvements;

[/list]

Thanks for checking out these notes and for playing!

Hello!

Sorry for the delay with this first update. This is just a small one for now. I plan on introducing more gameplay content in the next update (and some more achievements too)! Thank you for your support. :-)

[list]
[*]Custom key-binding in the controls menu;
[*]Improved how the measuring tape widget displays numbers;
[*]Some glitch fixing and a few improvements;
[*]New texture for the leaves on the trees (wow!);
[/list]
There is an option to reset all keys to default. There is still a bug or two I haven't squashed yet with the custom keys. Sometimes an additional default or previously removed key might be added when starting up Free Play. Reloading the area (or resetting to default a few times lol) gets rid of that glitched extra key. Will try to straighten that out very soon!

Also, due to how Unreal Engine handles input, it does not register mouse wheel scroll inputs when setting custom keys. If you change those inputs, the only current way to change them back to the mouse wheel is to reset to default controls. I'll attempt to find a work-around.
